  "worked_solution": "First, because the initial condition is $y(4)=-1,$ we fill $y=-1$ into the table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{\u2032}\\,$ | $\\,\u0394y\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $-1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{\u2032}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\u2032} & =\\sqrt{3x+4}+y \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3(4)+4}+(-1) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16}-1 \\\\  & =4-1 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{\u2032}\\,$ | $\\,\u0394y\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $-1$ | $3$ |  |\n\nNext, we compute $\u0394y$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0394y & ={y}^{\u2032}\\cdot \u0394x \\\\  & =3(1) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{\u2032}\\,$ | $\\,\u0394y\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $-1$ | $3$ | $3$ |\n\nTo get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the *next* row, we add $\u0394x$ to $x$ and $\u0394y$ to $y,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+\u0394x \\\\  & =4+1 \\\\  & =5 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\u0394y \\\\  & =-1+3 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these results to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{\u2032}\\,$ | $\\,\u0394y\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $-1$ | $3$ | $3$ |\n| $5$ | $2$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(5)\u22482.$",
